# Intent: Games item 3, the touch, voice and screen hooks (builds on G02). A game starts from the touch screen: quick settings, More, Games (a page with one button per game and its best score, in English or Spanish by the saved language); a refusal (full quiet, an update) is written on that page in plain words and the page stays. While a game runs the face's press handler passes it every touch that began outside the screen edges (the edges stay the unit's: the top swipe still opens quick settings, the side swipes still change the volume, the bottom swipe stops), no touch starts a listen, and no touch toggles mute, vision or full quiet. The bottom swipe ends a running game first and only otherwise aborts speech as before. The stop word ends a running game unless the unit is speaking (then it ends the speech, as before), after a ringing timer takes it first; the stop word is armed while a game runs (best effort, never while muted) and is not disarmed by a state change while a game runs. A game never moves the head: nothing here calls the motion code.
# Placement: unit (the screen and the stop word are on the robot)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc, firmware/main/hal/maipai_more.cc and firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/application.cc of this tree (MIT)
# Check after a flash: quick settings, More shows a Games button (Juegos in Spanish) and its page shows the three games; a game opens over the face, taps in its areas count, a tap in a screen edge does nothing to it, a swipe down from the bottom edge ends it, saying stop ends it while the unit is not speaking, and the face works as before afterwards (a tap on the mouth toggles mute, a tap elsewhere starts a listen). UNVERIFIED without a finger or a microphone: see docs/design/games-2026-11-16.md for what the bench drove instead.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_GAMES (G01); off leaves no Games button and no hook.
